{
  "case_id": "2008-07-9995",
  "document_hash": "48e58e46234583b304518604f33f8bad3661deae13049d059bbef67b199038cc",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-9995",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "48e58e46234583b304518604f33f8bad3661deae13049d059bbef67b199038cc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-48e58e462345-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:05 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-07-9995",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "48e58e46234583b304518604f33f8bad3661deae13049d059bbef67b199038cc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-48e58e462345-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Petitioner lawfully exercised a peremptory challenge on juror Delores Gomez. As a result of the erroneous denial of that challenge, Ms. Gomez wrongfully sat on the jury and lacked authority to render a judgment. Petitioner's conviction should be reversed automatically for three separate and independent reasons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-9995",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "48e58e46234583b304518604f33f8bad3661deae13049d059bbef67b199038cc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-48e58e462345-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Are you putting -- are you equating this with a biased judge? The -- the category of structural error has been kept very narrow by this Court. And it seems to me that a juror who is perfectly qualified, who it is conceded -- it is"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-9995",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "48e58e46234583b304518604f33f8bad3661deae13049d059bbef67b199038cc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-48e58e462345-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Okay. But your whole argument that the -- that the juror was illegally sitting and the jury was illegally constituted is a -- in effect a statement of the effect of State law. And the State supreme court doesn't think that's the effect under State law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-9995",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "48e58e46234583b304518604f33f8bad3661deae13049d059bbef67b199038cc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-48e58e462345-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: You don't need a good reason for a peremptory challenge."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-9995",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "48e58e46234583b304518604f33f8bad3661deae13049d059bbef67b199038cc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-48e58e462345-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Well, does it really?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. SCODRO",
      "case_id": "2008-07-9995",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "48e58e46234583b304518604f33f8bad3661deae13049d059bbef67b199038cc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-48e58e462345-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In those contexts, the very State law that has created those divisions, for whatever reason they have seen fit to do so, is the proper authority to conclude whether or not the error is so profound by having that person sit that it ought not be a violation of due process -- that it ought to be a void judgment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2008-07-9995",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "48e58e46234583b304518604f33f8bad3661deae13049d059bbef67b199038cc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-48e58e462345-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What happens in the situation where a juror -- where a juror should have been excused? I guess there's a new trial. The juror should have been excused, but wasn't."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Matthew D. Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-9995",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "48e58e46234583b304518604f33f8bad3661deae13049d059bbef67b199038cc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-48e58e462345-0002-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Federal law does not require automatic reversal of a conviction because the denial of a peremptory challenge at most violated only his State law rights. And even if his Federal constitutional rights had been violated, harmless error review would apply."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-9995",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "48e58e46234583b304518604f33f8bad3661deae13049d059bbef67b199038cc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-48e58e462345-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
